# foundry-01: a human + agent team. scribe (an agent) both speaks into the
# shared org scope (foundry-auth-e1) and keeps its own private scratch
# memory (scribe-e1, agent-scoped) - same actor, different scope per
# event, which is the point: scope is about who can see the event, not
# who wrote it. foundry-auth-e1/e2 also flips the usual authority
# hard-negative around: here it's an agent's suggestion, not a VP's, that
# must not outrank the human's later explicit decision.

